{"id":"mahabharata-3-045","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":45,"title":"पञ्चचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 45 · Lomasha is sent to the Pandavas","summary":{"en":"Arjuna lives in heaven, learning the use of divine weapons and music and dance from the Gandharva Chitrasena. The sage Lomasha, visiting Indra, sees Arjuna seated beside him, and Indra sends him to Yudhishthira with news of Arjuna and to guide the brothers on a pilgrimage.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದು ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಪ್ರಯೋಗವನ್ನೂ ಗಂಧರ್ವ ಚಿತ್ರಸೇನನಿಂದ ಸಂಗೀತ ನೃತ್ಯಗಳನ್ನೂ ಕಲಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಂದ್ರನನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾದ ಲೋಮಶ ಋಷಿ ಅವನ ಪಕ್ಕ ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಸುದ್ದಿ ತಿಳಿಸಿ ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನು ತೀರ್ಥಯಾತ್ರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಮುನ್ನಡೆಸಲು ಇಂದ್ರನು ಅವರನ್ನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन स्वर्ग में रहकर दिव्यास्त्रों का प्रयोग और गन्धर्व चित्रसेन से संगीत तथा नृत्य सीखते हैं। इन्द्र से मिलने आए ऋषि लोमश उनके पास अर्जुन को बैठे देखते हैं, और इन्द्र उन्हें अर्जुन का समाचार देने और भाइयों को तीर्थयात्रा में मार्गदर्शन देने के लिए युधिष्ठिर के पास भेजते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు స్వర్గంలో ఉండి దివ్యాస్త్ర ప్రయోగాన్ని, గంధర్వుడు చిత్రసేనుని నుండి సంగీత నృత్యాలను నేర్చుకుంటాడు. ఇంద్రుని సందర్శించిన లోమశ మహర్షి ఆయన పక్కన అర్జునుని చూస్తాడు; అర్జునుని వార్త చెప్పి సోదరులను తీర్థయాత్రలో నడిపించడానికి ఇంద్రుడు ఆయనను యుధిష్ఠిరుని వద్దకు పంపుతాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் ஸ்வர்க்கத்தில் தங்கித் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரப் பயன்பாட்டையும், கந்தர்வன் சித்ரஸேனனிடம் இசையும் நடனமும் கற்கிறான். இந்திரனைக் காண வந்த லோமஶ முனிவர் அவனருகே அர்ஜுனனைக் காண, அர்ஜுனனின் செய்தியைச் சொல்லவும் சகோதரர்களைத் தீர்த்தயாத்திரையில் வழிநடத்தவும் இந்திரன் அவரை யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் அனுப்புகிறான்.","ml":"സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽ വസിക്കുന്ന അർജുനൻ ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രവിദ്യയും ഗന്ധർവൻ ചിത്രസേനനിൽനിന്ന് സംഗീതവും നൃത്തവും പഠിക്കുന്നു. ഇന്ദ്രനെ കാണാൻ വന്ന ലോമശൻ മുനി അർജുനൻ ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ അരികിലിരിക്കുന്നത് കാണുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ വാർത്തയുമായി യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ അടുത്തേക്കും സഹോദരന്മാരെ തീർത്ഥയാത്രയിൽ നയിക്കാനും ഇന്ദ്രൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ അയക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.45; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो देवाः सगन्धर्वाः समादायार्घ्यमुत्तमम् ।\nशक्रस्य मतमाज्ञाय पार्थमानर्चुरञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gods and gandharvas, knowing Shakra's wish, brought the best arghya offering and quickly honored Partha."}},{"n":2,"text":"पाद्यमाचमनीयं च प्रतिग्राह्य नृपात्मजम् ।\nप्रवेशयामासुरथो पुरंदरनिवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having offered the prince water for the feet and for rinsing the mouth, they led him into Purandara's dwelling."}},{"n":3,"text":"एवं संपूजितो जिष्णुरुवास भवने पितुः ।\nउपशिक्षन्महास्त्राणि ससंहाराणि पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored thus, Jishnu lived in his father's house, the Pandava learning the great weapons with their withdrawal."}},{"n":4,"text":"शक्रस्य हस्ताद्दयितं वज्रमस्त्रं दुरुत्सहम् ।\nअशनीश्च महानादा मेघबर्हिणलक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Shakra's own hand he received the dear and irresistible thunderbolt weapon, and the thunderbolts with great roars, marked like peacocks and clouds."}},{"n":5,"text":"गृहीतास्त्रस्तु कौन्तेयो भ्रातॄन्सस्मार पाण्डवः ।\nपुरंदरनियोगाच्च पञ्चाब्दमवसत्सुखी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received the weapons, the Pandava, son of Kunti, remembered his brothers; yet at Purandara's command he lived there happily for five years."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः शक्रोऽब्रवीत्पार्थं कृतास्त्रं काल आगते ।\nनृत्तं गीतं च कौन्तेय चित्रसेनादवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when the time had come and the weapons were mastered, Shakra said to Partha: \"Learn dance and song, son of Kunti, from Chitrasena.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"वादित्रं देवविहितं नृलोके यन्न विद्यते ।\nतदर्जयस्व कौन्तेय श्रेयो वै ते भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Learn the instrumental music made by the gods, which is not known in the world of men, son of Kunti; it will be good for you.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सखायं प्रददौ चास्य चित्रसेनं पुरंदरः ।\nस तेन सह संगम्य रेमे पार्थो निरामयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Purandara gave Chitrasena to him as a friend, and Partha lived happily and free of care in his company."}},{"n":9,"text":"कदाचिदटमानस्तु महर्षिरुत लोमशः ।\nजगाम शक्रभवनं पुरंदरदिदृक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once the great sage Lomasha, wandering about, went to Shakra's house wishing to see Purandara."}},{"n":10,"text":"स समेत्य नमस्कृत्य देवराजं महामुनिः ।\nददर्शार्धासनगतं पाण्डवं वासवस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great sage, meeting and bowing to the king of the gods, saw the Pandava sitting on half of Vasava's seat."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः शक्राभ्यनुज्ञात आसने विष्टरोत्तरे ।\nनिषसाद द्विजश्रेष्ठः पूज्यमानो महर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, given leave by Shakra, the best of brahmins sat on a seat spread with kusha, honored by great sages."}},{"n":12,"text":"तस्य दृष्ट्वाभवद्बुद्धिः पार्थमिन्द्रासने स्थितम् ।\nकथं नु क्षत्रियः पार्थः शक्रासनमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Partha on Indra's seat, a thought arose in him: how could Partha, a warrior, have gained Shakra's seat?"}},{"n":13,"text":"किं त्वस्य सुकृतं कर्म लोका वा के विनिर्जिताः ।\nय एवमुपसंप्राप्तः स्थानं देवनमस्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What good deed did he do, or what worlds did he conquer, that he thus attained a place honored by the gods?"}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्य विज्ञाय संकल्पं शक्रो वृत्रनिषूदनः ।\nलोमशं प्रहसन्वाक्यमिदमाह शचीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his thought, Shakra, slayer of Vritra and husband of Shachi, said to Lomasha with a smile:"}},{"n":15,"text":"ब्रह्मर्षे श्रूयतां यत्ते मनसैतद्विवक्षितम् ।\nनायं केवलमर्त्यो वै क्षत्रियत्वमुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmin sage, hear what you wish to say in your mind: he has not come to the warrior's state as a mere mortal.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"महर्षे मम पुत्रोऽयं कुन्त्यां जातो महाभुजः ।\nअस्त्रहेतोरिह प्राप्तः कस्माच्चित्कारणान्तरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great sage, this mighty-armed son of mine, born of Kunti, has come here for weapons, for some other reason as well.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अहो नैनं भवान्वेत्ति पुराणमृषिसत्तमम् ।\nशृणु मे वदतो ब्रह्मन्योऽयं यच्चास्य कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ah, you do not know that he is an ancient best of sages. Hear from me, brahmin, as I tell who he is and the reason for his coming.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"नरनारायणौ यौ तौ पुराणावृषिसत्तमौ ।\nताविमावभिजानीहि हृषीकेशधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The two ancient best of sages, Nara and Narayana: know these two to be Hrishikesha and Dhananjaya.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"यन्न शक्यं सुरैर्द्रष्टुमृषिभिर्वा महात्मभिः ।\nतदाश्रमपदं पुण्यं बदरी नाम विश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That holy hermitage that gods and great sages cannot see, known as Badari,\""}},{"n":20,"text":"स निवासोऽभवद्विप्र विष्णोर्जिष्णोस्तथैव च ।\nयतः प्रववृते गङ्गा सिद्धचारणसेविता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"was the dwelling of Vishnu and of Jishnu, where the Ganga flowed forth, frequented by siddhas and charanas.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तौ मन्नियोगाद्ब्रह्मर्षे क्षितौ जातौ महाद्युती ।\nभूमेर्भारावतरणं महावीर्यौ करिष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At my command, brahmin sage, these two radiant ones were born on earth; being of great valor they will lift the burden of the earth.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"उद्वृत्ता ह्यसुराः केचिन्निवातकवचा इति ।\nविप्रियेषु स्थितास्माकं वरदानेन मोहिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Some arrogant asuras called Nivatakavachas, deluded by a boon, are set on being hostile to us.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तर्कयन्ते सुरान्हन्तुं बलदर्पसमन्विताः ।\nदेवान्न गणयन्ते च तथा दत्तवरा हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Proud of their strength, they plan to kill the gods, and having received boons they do not count the gods.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"पातालवासिनो रौद्रा दनोः पुत्रा महाबलाः ।\nसर्वे देवनिकाया हि नालं योधयितुं स्म तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The terrible, mighty sons of Danu, who live in Patala, are such that all the hosts of the gods are not enough to fight them.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"योऽसौ भूमिगतः श्रीमान्विष्णुर्मधुनिषूदनः ।\nकपिलो नाम देवोऽसौ भगवानजितो हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The glorious Vishnu, slayer of Madhu, who has come to earth, is the god named Kapila, the blessed, unconquered Hari,\""}},{"n":26,"text":"येन पूर्वं महात्मानः खनमाना रसातलम् ।\nदर्शनादेव निहताः सगरस्यात्मजा विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"by whom long ago the great-souled sons of Sagara, digging toward Rasatala, were slain merely by his glance, lord.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तेन कार्यं महत्कार्यमस्माकं द्विजसत्तम ।\nपार्थेन च महायुद्धे समेताभ्यामसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With him, best of brahmins, and with Partha, joined together in a great battle, our great task will undoubtedly be done.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"अयं तेषां समस्तानां शक्तः प्रतिसमासने ।\nतान्निहत्य रणे शूरः पुनर्यास्यति मानुषान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This one is able to face all of them; having slain them in battle, the hero will return to the mortals.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"भवांश्चास्मन्नियोगेन यातु तावन्महीतलम् ।\nकाम्यके द्रक्ष्यसे वीरं निवसन्तं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And you, by our command, go for now to the surface of the earth; in Kamyaka you will see the hero Yudhishthira living.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"स वाच्यो मम संदेशाद्धर्मात्मा सत्यसंगरः ।\nनोत्कण्ठा फल्गुने कार्या कृतास्त्रः शीघ्रमेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You should tell that righteous one, true to his word, from me: 'Do not be anxious for Phalguna; he has mastered the weapons and will come quickly.'\""}},{"n":31,"text":"नाशुद्धबाहुवीर्येण नाकृतास्त्रेण वा रणे ।\nभीष्मद्रोणादयो युद्धे शक्याः प्रतिसमासितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Without arms purified in strength and without mastery of weapons, Bhishma, Drona and the others cannot be faced in battle.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"गृहीतास्त्रो गुडाकेशो महाबाहुर्महामनाः ।\nनृत्तवादित्रगीतानां दिव्यानां पारमेयिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gudakesha, great-armed and great-minded, having gained the weapons, has reached the far shore of the divine arts of dance, instruments and song.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"भवानपि विविक्तानि तीर्थानि मनुजेश्वर ।\nभ्रातृभिः सहितः सर्वैर्द्रष्टुमर्हत्यरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And you, ruler of men, scourge of foes, should visit secluded holy places together with all your brothers.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"तीर्थेष्वाप्लुत्य पुण्येषु विपाप्मा विगतज्वरः ।\nराज्यं भोक्ष्यसि राजेन्द्र सुखी विगतकल्मषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bathing in the holy bathing places, free of sin and fever, O king of kings, you will enjoy your kingdom happily and cleansed of stain.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"भवांश्चैनं द्विजश्रेष्ठ पर्यटन्तं महीतले ।\nत्रातुमर्हति विप्राग्र्य तपोबलसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And you, best of brahmins, rich in the power of austerity, should protect him as he travels the earth.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"गिरिदुर्गेषु हि सदा देशेषु विषमेषु च ।\nवसन्ति राक्षसा रौद्रास्तेभ्यो रक्षेत्सदा भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For in mountain fastnesses and rough regions terrible rakshasas always dwell; you should always guard him from them.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"स तथेति प्रतिज्ञाय लोमशः सुमहातपाः ।\nकाम्यकं वनमुद्दिश्य समुपायान्महीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha, of great austerity, promising, \"So be it,\" descended to earth, heading for the Kamyaka forest."}},{"n":38,"text":"ददर्श तत्र कौन्तेयं धर्मराजमरिंदमम् ।\nतापसैर्भ्रातृभिश्चैव सर्वतः परिवारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, the scourge of enemies, surrounded on all sides by ascetics and his brothers."}}]}]}